  "notes": "{築|きず}く means to build or construct, used for both physical structures and abstract achievements.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle: ～を{築|きず}く\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {城|しろ}を{築|きず}く: to build a castle\n- {関係|かんけい}を{築|きず}く: to build a relationship\n- {財産|ざいさん}を{築|きず}く: to build wealth\n- {地位|ちい}を{築|きず}く: to establish a position\n- キャリアを{築|きず}く: to build a career\n- {人脈|じんみゃく}を{築|きず}く: to build a network\n\nDON'T CONFUSE:\n- {築|きず}く (godan): to build\n- {気|き}づく (godan): to notice (different kanji and meaning)\n\nThe physical sense often appears in historical or literary contexts; the abstract sense is common in business and personal development.",
